== 8. Size of the inertia change in a velocity-gated Newtonian potential: eps = 2 beta |Phi|/v*^2 (v* = 120 km/s)
  Earth around the Sun, |Phi| = v_orb^2, v_orb = 29.8 km/s    : eps/beta = 0.123
  Milky Way at the Sun, |Phi| ~ v_c^2, v_c = 230 km/s         : eps/beta = 7.347
  classical dwarf, |Phi| ~ 3 sigma^2, sigma = 10 km/s         : eps/beta = 0.042
  ultra-faint dwarf, |Phi| ~ 3 sigma^2, sigma = 3.7 km/s      : eps/beta = 0.006
  co-moving fraction in the MW halo (sigma = 155 km/s), n_gate/n = (v*/sigma)^3/(2 pi)^1.5 = 0.029; eps/beta with only that fraction gated = 0.216
  inertia singularity of the Lagrangian form, r_* = 2 beta GM/v*^2, for the Sun (beta = 1): 0.123 AU

